Subject: [PATCH] feat: show conduit fill % on the Duct Bank Runs table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second iteration of the Conduit section (see claude/plan-seccion-ducteria.md):
surfaces fill_percentage/spare_capacity that fiber_routes already computes
at route creation, as a progress bar per run, flagged past the conventional
40% pullability ceiling for communications cable. No schema change and no
new calculation engine yet — this reuses data the app already produces.

- getConduitData(): joins in fiber_routes.fill_percentage/spare_capacity.
- ConduitPageClient: new Fill % column with a FillBar meter, an "Avg.
  Conduit Fill" summary card that highlights amber when any run is over
  threshold, and a one-line explainer under the page header.

Still open from the roadmap: a dedicated cross-section/duct-view (bigger,
separate follow-up) and a fill % calc that sums ALL cables sharing a run
instead of the single cable recorded at route creation.
